# Generated from the service's own spec by scripts/spec-sync/sync.rb.
# Do not edit this file: change the spec in the service repo instead.
openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: Skylit Public API
  version: "1.1.0"
  summary: Options-Greeks heatmaps as a public HTTP API.
  description: |
    Skylit exposes its real-time options-Greeks (gamma / vanna) heatmaps as a
    versioned public HTTP API, per strike, with the live velocity metric and
    Skylit's node classification (King / Gatekeeper / etc.).

    **Authentication.** Send your Skylit API key as a bearer token:

        Authorization: Bearer <key>

    A request without an `Authorization` header gets `401`; an invalid,
    revoked or expired key gets `403`.

    The gateway also accepts the bare key in the same header
    (`Authorization: <key>`); `Bearer` is the documented form. The key is not
    read from `X-API-Key` or the query string: those requests get `401`.

    **Credit metering.** Every chargeable request debits a fixed cost from
    your credit balance:

    | Endpoint        | Cost |
    |-----------------|-----:|
    | `/v1/heatmap`    | 1   |
    | `/v1/gex/levels` | 1   |
    | `/v1/historical` | 5   |
    | `/v1/historical/range` | 25 |
    | `/v1/stats/daily` | 5  |
    | `/v1/stream`     | 1 per symbol to open + 1 per symbol per minute open |
    | `/v1/account`, `/v1/symbols`, `/v1/openapi.json` | 0 |

    `/v1/openapi.json` (this document) needs no key.

    **Failed calls are free:** a request answered with any 4xx or 5xx status is
    refunded, and its `X-Credits-Remaining` already reflects the refund.

    New API accounts start with 5,000 credits; Pro, Protégé and Quant also get
    25,000 included credits each month (`GET /v1/account` shows the balance).
    Every chargeable response
    carries `X-Credits-Remaining: <balance>`. Out of credits → `402`
    `insufficient_credits`; an admin-suspended account → `403`
    `account_suspended`. Top up via your account console.

    **Rate limits.** Each key has a requests-per-minute limit set by the
    account's plan (Pro, Protégé and Quant: 120 per key; invite: 60 per key),
    counted across every Skylit API host. `GET /v1/account` returns it as
    `limits.requestsPerMinute`; read it instead of hard-coding a number. Over
    it the gateway answers `429` `rate_limited`. Responses carry
    `X-RateLimit-Limit` (the key's limit), `X-RateLimit-Remaining` (requests
    left in the current window) and `X-RateLimit-Reset` (Unix time, in
    seconds, when the window resets). The gateway's `429` has no `Retry-After`: wait until
    `X-RateLimit-Reset`. `429`s from the API itself (concurrency and stream
    limits) carry `Retry-After`.

    **Attribution.** Every response carries
    `X-Skylit-Attribution: Data: Skylit (https://skylit.ai/?utm_source=api&utm_medium=attribution)`, JSON success
    responses carry `meta.attribution`, and `/v1/stream`'s `connected` event
    carries the same object. When you share or publish Skylit data, credit
    "Data: Skylit" (https://www.skylit.ai/api-terms#attribution).

    **Symbols.** Multi-symbol routes take at most 10 distinct symbols per
    request; more is a `400` `invalid_parameter` (never silently truncated).
    Unknown symbols in a list are omitted from `data.symbols`; if none of the
    requested symbols is available the response is `404` `symbol_not_found`.

    Live streams (`/v1/stream`) cost 1 credit per symbol to open plus 1 per
    symbol per minute connected, and close after one hour.

    **Resolution.** The heatmap is a 1-second time series. `/v1/heatmap` and
    `/v1/historical` return the single snapshot at or before the requested
    instant (`/v1/historical` to the second); `/v1/historical/range` returns
    every snapshot in a window of up to 15 minutes. History goes back to
    2023-03-28; `meta.resolution` reports the resolution actually served:
    `"1s"`, or `"1m"` for the older history that is only stored once a minute.

    **Board size.** By default `/v1/heatmap` returns 92 strikes around spot
    and the nearest 5 expirations, and leaves out interior strikes whose cells
    are all negligible. `maxStrikes=all&maxExpirations=all&includeEmpty=true`
    returns the full board exactly as stored. Limits above a cap are a `400`,
    never a silent reduction.

    **Compression.** Send `Accept-Encoding: gzip` and JSON responses come back
    gzip-compressed (typically 3-5x smaller). Streams are never compressed.

    **Velocity is live-only.** The `velocityPct` field is present on
    `/v1/heatmap` (live) and absent on `/v1/historical` (replay).

    **Response shape.** Success → `{ "data": ..., "meta": { ... } }`; errors →
    `{ "error": { "code": "...", "message": "..." } }`, including the ones
    the gateway sends itself (`401`, `403`, `429`, `504`). Unknown paths are
    `404` `not_found`. camelCase throughout.
    `data.symbols` is always an array (one element per requested symbol), so a
    single-symbol call and a multi-symbol "Trinity" call share one shape.

servers:
  - url: https://api.skylit.ai
    description: Production

security:
  - bearerApiKey: []

tags:
  - name: Heatmap
  - name: Tempest
    description: |
      Tempest, Skylit's volatility suite: implied vol per symbol (SVX), term
      structure, expected-move cones, sigma move tracking, surface and skew,
      call/put premium tilt, event vol and VRP, the S&P volatility complex, a
      universe screener and daily history. Precomputed by Tempest; every
      response states when (`asOf`) and for which session (`sessionDate`).
      In preview: `403 not_entitled` until enabled for your account.

      These endpoints serve derived analytics only: implied vols, skews,
      ratios, z-scores, ranks and percent moves. Option prices and price
      levels read from option quotes (contract mids, straddle prices or moves,
      forwards, the VIX-forward curve) are not part of any /v1/vol response.
  - name: Meta

paths:
  /v1/heatmap:
    get:
      summary: Live per-strike heatmap (one or more symbols)
      operationId: getHeatmap
      x-credits: 1
      tags: [Heatmap]
      description: |
        Current per-strike heatmap for one or more symbols at the latest
        snapshot. Includes the live `velocityPct` per strike. Pass multiple
        comma-separated symbols for a single cross-asset call (the app's
        Trinity is `SPXW,SPY,QQQ`; `SPX` is the monthlies only), and
        `expirations` to net each strike over specific expiration dates instead
        of the nearest `maxExpirations`. A call that cannot finish within 20
        seconds answers `504` `gateway_timeout` (refunded); retry, or request
        fewer symbols.
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Symbols"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Metric"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxStrikes"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxExpirations"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/IncludeEmpty"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Expirations"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Layout"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Live heatmap snapshot(s).
          headers:
            Cache-Control: { schema: { type: string, example: "private, max-age=5" } }
            X-RateLimit-Limit: { schema: { type: integer } }
            X-RateLimit-Remaining: { schema: { type: integer } }
            X-RateLimit-Reset: { schema: { type: integer } }
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required: [data, meta]
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: object
                    required: [symbols]
                    properties:
                      symbols:
                        type: array
                        items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/SymbolHeatmap" }
                  meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Meta" }
              examples:
                live:
                  summary: SPY live (truncated)
                  value:
                    data:
                      symbols:
                        - symbol: SPY
                          asOf: "2026-05-22T14:31:00Z"
                          spot: 591.23
                          previousClose: 589.10
                          priceChange: 2.13
                          priceChangePercent: 0.36
                          expirations: ["2026-05-22", "2026-05-23", "2026-05-30"]
                          strikes:
                            - { strike: 590, value: 1894300.4, nodeType: king, velocityPct: 12.4 }
                            - { strike: 595, value: 642100.2, nodeType: gatekeeper, velocityPct: -3.1 }
                            - { strike: 585, value: 88010.0, nodeType: normal, velocityPct: 0.4 }
                    meta: { metric: gamma, resolution: "1s", mode: live, cached: false }
                singleExpiration:
                  summary: SPY netted over one expiration (`expirations=2026-05-23`)
                  value:
                    data:
                      symbols:
                        - symbol: SPY
                          asOf: "2026-05-22T14:31:00Z"
                          spot: 591.23
                          previousClose: 589.10
                          priceChange: 2.13
                          priceChangePercent: 0.36
                          expirations: ["2026-05-23"]
                          strikes:
                            - { strike: 590, value: 412880.1, nodeType: king, velocityPct: 8.2 }
                            - { strike: 595, value: 121400.7, nodeType: gatekeeper, velocityPct: -1.4 }
                    meta: { metric: gamma, resolution: "1s", mode: live, cached: false }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }

  /v1/historical:
    get:
      summary: Replay — per-strike heatmap at a past instant (one or more symbols)
      operationId: getHistoricalHeatmap
      x-credits: 5
      tags: [Heatmap]
      description: |
        The latest snapshot at or before `at` for one or more symbols — same
        shape as `/v1/heatmap` minus `velocityPct` (velocity is live-only),
        including `layout=matrix` for the per-expiration grid. Precision is
        1 second where 1-second history exists for that day and 1 minute
        otherwise; `meta.resolution` says which. `at` may go back to
        2023-03-28, where heatmap history begins (coverage per symbol varies;
        `/v1/symbols` lists each symbol's first date). If no snapshot exists
        at/near that instant the response is `404` with `code: no_data`.
        A read that cannot finish within 20 seconds answers `504`
        `gateway_timeout` (refunded); retry, or request fewer symbols.
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Symbols"
        - name: at
          in: query
          required: true
          description: RFC3339 instant to replay (e.g. `2026-03-05T10:01:00Z`). Not before 2023-03-28.
          schema: { type: string, format: date-time }
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Metric"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxStrikes"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxExpirations"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/IncludeEmpty"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Expirations"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Layout"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Historical heatmap snapshot(s).
          headers:
            X-RateLimit-Limit: { schema: { type: integer } }
            X-RateLimit-Remaining: { schema: { type: integer } }
            X-RateLimit-Reset: { schema: { type: integer } }
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required: [data, meta]
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: object
                    required: [symbols]
                    properties:
                      symbols:
                        type: array
                        items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/SymbolHeatmap" }
                  meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Meta" }
              examples:
                replay:
                  summary: SPY at a past minute (truncated)
                  value:
                    data:
                      symbols:
                        - symbol: SPY
                          asOf: "2026-03-05T10:01:00Z"
                          spot: 512.40
                          previousClose: 510.02
                          priceChange: 2.38
                          priceChangePercent: 0.47
                          expirations: ["2026-03-05", "2026-03-06"]
                          strikes:
                            - { strike: 512, value: 1500200.0, nodeType: king }
                            - { strike: 515, value: 410000.0, nodeType: gatekeeper }
                    meta: { metric: gamma, resolution: "1s", mode: historical, cached: false }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        "404":
          description: |
            No snapshot at/near the requested instant, none of the requested
            symbols is available, or none of the requested `expirations` exist
            in that snapshot.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" }
              examples:
                symbolNotFound:
                  value: { error: { code: symbol_not_found, message: "Symbol \"ZZZZQ\" is not available." } }
                noData:
                  value: { error: { code: no_data, message: "No snapshot available for SPY at 2025-01-01T10:01:00Z." } }
                expirationNotFound:
                  value:
                    error:
                      code: expiration_not_found
                      message: "None of the requested expirations are available for SPY. Available: 2026-03-05, 2026-03-06, 2026-03-07."
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }

  /v1/historical/range:
    get:
      summary: Replay — every snapshot in a window (up to 15 minutes, 5 symbols)
      operationId: getHistoricalRange
      x-credits: 25
      tags: [Heatmap]
      description: |
        Every snapshot between `from` and `to` (inclusive) for up to 5
        symbols, at the stored resolution — one per second where 1-second
        history exists (`meta.resolution: "1s"`), otherwise one per minute.
        Each frame's `values[i]` is the net exposure at
        `axes[frame.axis].strikes[i]`, summed over that axis's expirations —
        the same number `/v1/historical` reports as `strikes[i].value` for
        that instant. Axes are listed once and referenced by id; a new axis
        appears only when the visible strikes or expirations change (the
        strike window follows spot). Plain JSON numbers; responses are
        gzip-compressed when the request sends `Accept-Encoding: gzip`.

        **Cost:** 25 credits per call.
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Symbols"
        - name: from
          in: query
          required: true
          description: RFC3339 start of the window (inclusive). Up to 365 days back.
          schema: { type: string, format: date-time }
        - name: to
          in: query
          required: true
          description: RFC3339 end of the window (inclusive). At most 15 minutes after `from`, not in the future.
          schema: { type: string, format: date-time }
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Metric"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxStrikes"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxExpirations"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Expirations"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Every snapshot in the window, per symbol.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required: [data, meta]
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: object
                    required: [from, to, symbols]
                    properties:
                      from: { type: string, format: date-time }
                      to: { type: string, format: date-time }
                      symbols:
                        type: array
                        items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/SymbolRange" }
                  meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Meta" }
              examples:
                range:
                  summary: SPY, two seconds (truncated)
                  value:
                    data:
                      from: "2026-03-05T14:30:00Z"
                      to: "2026-03-05T14:30:01Z"
                      symbols:
                        - symbol: SPY
                          axes:
                            - { id: 0, strikes: [510, 512, 515], expirations: ["2026-03-05", "2026-03-06"] }
                          frames:
                            - { asOf: "2026-03-05T14:30:00.000Z", axis: 0, spot: 512.40, previousClose: 510.02, values: [88010.0, 1500200.0, 410000.0] }
                            - { asOf: "2026-03-05T14:30:01.000Z", axis: 0, spot: 512.43, previousClose: 510.02, values: [87120.5, 1502113.2, 409877.1] }
                    meta: { metric: gamma, resolution: "1s", mode: historical, cached: false }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unavailable" }

  /v1/stream:
    get:
      summary: Live SSE stream (up to 10 symbols per connection)
      operationId: streamHeatmap
      x-credits: 1
      x-credits-per-minute: 1
      tags: [Heatmap]
      description: |
        A **Server-Sent Events** (`text/event-stream`) feed of live per-strike
        heatmaps. Two wire formats:

        - **v2** (default with `symbols=`, or `format=v2`): up to 10 symbols on
          one connection, camelCase events matching `SymbolHeatmap`, resumable
          with `Last-Event-ID`.
        - **v1** (default with `symbol=`): the original single-symbol format,
          unchanged.

        ### v2 events

        Every event names its `symbol` (except connection-level events).

        | Event | `id:` | Payload |
        |---|---|---|
        | `connected` | — | `{format:"v2", symbols, metric, creditsRemaining, creditsPerMinute, maxDurationSeconds}` |
        | `resumed` | yes | Only when `Last-Event-ID` was sent. See *Resume*. |
        | `snapshot` | yes | `StreamSnapshot` (= `SymbolHeatmap` + `lagged`). Once per symbol on connect, then on every board change. |
        | `velocity` | yes | `StreamVelocity`: per-node velocity for the stream's `metric`, when it changes (checked every ~3s). |
        | `symbol_unavailable` | — | `{symbol, reason: "no_live_board" \| "expiration_not_found", message}`; a `snapshot` follows once a board exists. |
        | `credits` | — | `{remaining, charged}` after each per-minute debit. |
        | `closed` | — | `{reason: "insufficient_credits" \| "account_suspended" \| "key_revoked" \| "monthly_cap_reached" \| "credit_check_failed"}`; stream ends. `key_revoked`: an API key on the account was revoked after this stream opened (streams opened on another still-valid key close too; reconnect to continue). `monthly_cap_reached`: the account's monthly spend cap was reached. |
        | `reconnect` | yes | `{reason: "max_duration" \| "server_shutdown"}`; stream ends, reconnect with `Last-Event-ID`. |
        | `: ping` | — | SSE comment every 15s so idle proxies (CloudFront: 60s) keep the connection. |

        Snapshots differ from `/v1/heatmap` in two ways: `spot` is the board's
        own spot, and strikes carry no `velocityPct` (use the `velocity`
        event). Within a symbol, `asOf` never goes backwards; a board already
        sent is never re-sent.

        **Event ids (resume cursor).** The `id:` is the connection's position
        in **every** symbol, not just the event's: a comma-separated list of
        `SYMBOL:asOfUnixMs`, e.g. `SPY:1790000000123,QQQ:1790000000456`.
        `asOfUnixMs` is the board's publish timestamp, identical on every
        server, so a cursor resumes on any pod. Per symbol it never decreases
        and strictly increases with each `snapshot` for that symbol.

        **Resume.** Reconnect with header `Last-Event-ID: <last id>` (browsers'
        `EventSource` does this automatically) or `?lastEventId=`. The server
        keeps no event history: boards are full state, so it sends the
        `resumed` event and then a fresh `snapshot` for every symbol that has a
        live board, whether or not it changed. Per symbol `status` is:
        `unchanged` (no board was published during the gap — nothing missed),
        `advanced` (at least one board was published; intermediate boards are
        **not** replayed, only the latest), `unknown` (symbol not in the
        cursor), or `unavailable` (no live board right now). `gapCovered` is
        true only if every symbol is `unchanged`; `stateRestored` is true when
        every symbol received a current snapshot. Velocity is not replayed; the
        latest reading is re-sent when this server has one.

        **Backpressure.** A client that reads slower than boards are published
        is never queued behind: each symbol holds at most one pending board, a
        newer board replaces it, and the board that is finally sent carries
        `lagged: true`. A client that stops reading for 30s is disconnected.

        **Pricing (v2).** `N` = number of symbols. `N` credits on connect
        (charged before the SSE upgrade, so an under-funded client gets a clean
        `402`), then `N` credits per minute open — 1 credit ($0.001) per symbol
        per minute, i.e. $0.06 per symbol-hour, plus $0.001 per symbol to open.
        Minutes are charged in advance and a partial minute is not refunded.

        **Limits.** At most 10 symbols per connection (more → `400`). At most
        25 symbols per customer per server across all open streams (a v1
        stream counts as 1); over it → `429` `stream_limit_reached` with
        `Retry-After: 2` (a just-closed stream frees its symbols within about
        a second). v1 also keeps its 5-streams cap. Each server streams a
        bounded number of **distinct** symbols across all customers (default
        20); a v2 stream that would add a new symbol beyond that gets `503`
        `stream_capacity` with `Retry-After: 5` — retry (you may land on
        another server). Symbols already being streamed are always admitted.
        Streams end after 1 hour with `reconnect`.

        ### v1 events (single symbol, unchanged)

        `connected` `{symbol, creditsRemaining}`, `initial_data`,
        `snapshot_update`, `velocity_update` (internal PascalCase board shape),
        `credits`, `closed`, `reconnect`, and a `: keepalive` comment every
        30s. 1 credit to open + 1 per minute. v1 rejects `expirations`.

        > OpenAPI cannot fully model an event stream. See
        > https://www.skylit.ai/docs/api-reference/rate-limits-and-retries (Streams).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Comma-separated tickers, up to 10 (e.g. `SPY,QQQ,IWM`). Selects format v2 by default. Unknown symbols → `404`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "SPY,QQQ,IWM" }
        - name: symbol
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Single ticker. Selects the legacy v1 format unless `format=v2`. Send `symbol` or `symbols`, not both.
          schema: { type: string, example: SPY }
        - name: format
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Wire format. Defaults to `v2` with `symbols=` and `v1` with `symbol=`. `v1` is single-symbol only.
          schema: { type: string, enum: [v1, v2] }
        - name: lastEventId
          in: query
          required: false
          description: v2 resume cursor, for clients that cannot set the `Last-Event-ID` header. The header wins if both are sent.
          schema: { type: string, example: "SPY:1790000000123,QQQ:1790000000456" }
        - name: Last-Event-ID
          in: header
          required: false
          description: v2 resume cursor — the last `id:` received.
          schema: { type: string }
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Metric"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxStrikes"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxExpirations"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/IncludeEmpty"
        - name: expirations
          in: query
          required: false
          description: v2 only — same meaning as on `/v1/heatmap`. Rejected with `400` on v1.
          schema: { type: string, example: "2026-05-22,2026-05-29" }
        - name: layout
          in: query
          required: false
          description: v2 only — `matrix` adds the per-expiration grid to each snapshot, as on `/v1/heatmap`.
          schema: { type: string, enum: [net, matrix], default: net }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: An SSE stream of heatmap events.
          content:
            text/event-stream:
              schema:
                type: string
                description: |
                  v2 frames, e.g.

                      event: snapshot
                      id: SPY:1790000000123,QQQ:1790000000456
                      data: {StreamSnapshot}

                  `snapshot` data matches #/components/schemas/StreamSnapshot,
                  `velocity` data #/components/schemas/StreamVelocity, and
                  `resumed` data #/components/schemas/StreamResumed.
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unavailable" }

  /v1/gex/levels:
    get:
      operationId: getLevels
      x-credits: 1
      summary: Key levels (classified nodes) for one or more symbols
      description: |
        The strikes Skylit classifies as nodes (king, gatekeeper, pika, barney,
        significant) for up to 10 symbols, strongest first, with each level's
        distance from spot. Same live source, filters and 5-second cache as
        `/v1/heatmap`; 1 credit per request.

        Each symbol also carries `summary`: total net exposure, the strongest
        positive and negative strikes (the walls), and the flip level where
        cumulative net exposure changes sign. It is computed from the strikes
        this request returned, so widen `maxStrikes` for a wider view.

        A call that cannot finish within 20 seconds answers `504`
        `gateway_timeout` (refunded); retry, or request fewer symbols.
      tags: [Heatmap]
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Symbols"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Metric"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxStrikes"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/MaxExpirations"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/IncludeEmpty"
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Expirations"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Levels per symbol.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: object
                    properties:
                      symbols:
                        type: array
                        items:
                          type: object
                          properties:
                            symbol: { type: string }
                            asOf: { type: string, format: date-time }
                            spot: { type: number }
                            previousClose: { type: number }
                            kingNode:
                              description: The strongest king node, or null when none is classified.
                              nullable: true
                              allOf:
                                - $ref: "#/components/schemas/Level"
                            levels:
                              type: array
                              items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Level" }
                            summary: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/LevelsSummary" }
                  meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Meta" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/account:
    get:
      operationId: getAccount
      x-credits: 0
      summary: Your balance and limits
      description: |
        The calling key's account: status, balance (credits and US dollars at
        $0.001 per credit), whether usage is unlimited, and the limits that
        apply. Free.
      tags: [Account]
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Account.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: object
                    properties:
                      customerId: { type: string }
                      status: { type: string, enum: [active, suspended] }
                      apiEligible: { type: boolean }
                      unlimited: { type: boolean }
                      creditsBalance: { type: integer }
                      balanceUsd: { type: number }
                      limits:
                        type: object
                        properties:
                          requestsPerMinute: { type: integer }
                          symbolsPerHeatmapCall: { type: integer }
                          symbolsPerStream: { type: integer }
                          streamSymbolsConcurrent:
                            type: integer
                            description: Symbols you may hold open at once across all streams (per server).
                          historicalInFlight: { type: integer }
                          activeKeys: { type: integer }
                          streamMaxDurationMinutes: { type: integer }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
  /v1/stats/daily:
    get:
      operationId: getDailyStats
      x-credits: 5
      summary: Daily statistics per symbol (ranking and spot range)
      tags: [Heatmap]
      description: |
        Per symbol and US trading session (ET): board spot open/high/low/close,
        the smallest and largest single cell of the session, and the mean and
        maximum over the session's frames of `max(|smallest cell|, |largest cell|)`
        (a measure of how concentrated the exposure is, useful for ranking a
        universe). Computed from 1-minute history, so every frame is one minute
        apart (`frames` counts them). Weight `peakAbsMean` by `frames` to
        average across days.

        **Sessions.** `date` is the ET session date. By default a row covers
        the regular session, 09:30-16:00 ET (frames stamped 09:30 up to
        15:59); `extended=true` covers 04:00-20:00 ET instead, including
        pre- and post-market. Weekends and NYSE market holidays have no
        session and no row, including for indices whose heatmap updates
        around the clock (SPX, SPXW, NDX, VIX). On early-close days the
        session simply has fewer frames. `firstAt`/`lastAt` are UTC
        timestamps. Today's row has `complete: false` until 30 minutes after
        the session ends, and changes as the session goes on.

        Up to 50 symbols, 31 calendar days and 400 symbol-sessions (symbols x
        trading days) per call. Sessions with no data are omitted; a symbol
        with none is omitted. Served from the historical file store; finished
        sessions are cached, so repeat and overlapping calls are fast.
        **Cost:** 5 credits per call.
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated tickers (up to 50).
          schema: { type: string, example: "SPY,QQQ,NVDA" }
        - name: from
          in: query
          required: true
          description: First session date (`YYYY-MM-DD`, ET), not before 2023-03-28.
          schema: { type: string, format: date }
        - name: to
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Last session date (`YYYY-MM-DD`, ET), inclusive. Default today (ET); at most 31 calendar days after `from`.
          schema: { type: string, format: date }
        - name: extended
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Cover the extended session (04:00-20:00 ET) instead of the regular session (09:30-16:00 ET).
          schema: { type: boolean, default: false }
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Metric"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Daily statistics.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required: [data, meta]
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: object
                    required: [from, to, symbols]
                    properties:
                      from: { type: string, format: date }
                      to: { type: string, format: date }
                      symbols:
                        type: array
                        items:
                          type: object
                          required: [symbol, days]
                          properties:
                            symbol: { type: string }
                            days:
                              type: array
                              items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/DailyStat" }
                  meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Meta" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/symbols:
    get:
      operationId: listSymbols
      x-credits: 0
      summary: Symbol catalog
      tags: [Meta]
      description: |
        Every symbol the API serves: whether it is an index, previous tickers
        after a rename (still accepted as input), the metrics available, and
        the UTC dates its history covers (`null` when coverage could not be
        read). History dates are refreshed every few hours. Free.
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Symbol catalog.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required: [data]
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: object
                    required: [symbols]
                    properties:
                      symbols:
                        type: array
                        items:
                          type: object
                          required: [symbol, isIndex, metrics, history]
                          properties:
                            symbol: { type: string }
                            isIndex: { type: boolean }
                            previousNames:
                              type: array
                              items: { type: string }
                            metrics:
                              type: array
                              items: { type: string, enum: [gamma, vanna] }
                            history:
                              type: object
                              nullable: true
                              required: [from, to]
                              properties:
                                from: { type: string, format: date }
                                to: { type: string, format: date }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unavailable" }
  /v1/vol/iv:
    get:
      operationId: getVolIv
      x-credits: 1
      summary: Implied volatility (SVX) per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        SVX, Tempest's constant-maturity implied volatility per symbol (a VIX-style
        variance-strip reading on the symbol's own option chain), in annualised vol
        points: `svx1d`, `svx9`, `svx30`, `svx3m`, `svx6m`, each also weekend-adjusted
        (`*_adj`, the weekly calendar pattern removed). Plus IV rank and percentile
        (`iv_rank`, `iv_pct`, over the trailing year, on the adjusted reading),
        1y/3y/5y percentiles per tenor (`pct_by`), the one-year range, the ratio to the
        VIX (`ratio_vix`, `ratio_z`), term slope and curve state, and historical
        mean-reversion odds (`reversion`). `quality` / `thin` flag shallow chains.
        Response: `data.symbols[]` has `symbol`, `asOf`, `sessionDate`, `stale` and `iv`.
        Symbols Tempest does not cover are listed in `data.missing`. **Cost:** 1 credit per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/term:
    get:
      operationId: getVolTerm
      x-credits: 1
      summary: Implied-volatility term structure per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        The symbol's implied-volatility term structure: one row per listed expiry
        used (days to expiry and the implied vol there), for contango/backwardation
        reads. The headline slope and curve state are in `/v1/vol/iv`.
        Optional `term.earnings_context` describes scheduled earnings exposure in the
        calendar-day 9-day and 30-day readings. `overlap_9d` and `overlap_30d` are
        `none` (before the known report), `partial` (spans the report), `full`
        (includes it), or null (unavailable). A report beyond nine days can already
        overlap the 9-day reading. This does not attribute premium or predict a flip.
        `date` and `timing` (`bmo` / `amc`) describe the recorded report, which can
        change; `within_9d` is nullable. `status` is `scheduled`, `limited`,
        `calendar_unavailable`, `no_report`, `timing_unknown`, or `report_passed`.
        Missing fields and nulls must not be treated as `none`.
        Response: `data.symbols[]` has `symbol`, `asOf`, `sessionDate`, `stale` and `term`.
        Symbols Tempest does not cover are listed in `data.missing`. **Cost:** 1 credit per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/cones:
    get:
      operationId: getVolCones
      x-credits: 1
      summary: Expected-move cones per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Tempest Cones: the move the options market prices for each horizon
        (`close`, `1d`, `week`, `opex`, `30d`), as 1-sigma percent and price bands
        around spot (from implied variance), plus the level set drawn on the
        chart. A horizon that does not exist at that moment (the `close`
        horizon after hours) is null.
        **Two different questions.** `horizons[]` is priced from the current
        spot: how much further options price the move from *now* to each
        settle. It moves with price, so it is not a budget to measure a move
        against. `levels[]` is priced at a past close and does not move
        intraday: read how far a move has gone against `hi1` / `lo1` (1-sigma)
        and `hi2` / `lo2` (2-sigma).

        **Levels** (`levels[]`): `day` (the prior close, to today's close),
        `week` (last week's final close, to this week's last close) and `month`
        (the last monthly options expiration's close, to the next monthly
        expiration's close). Each has `name`, `label`, `anchor`, `priced_at`,
        `until`, `em1_pct` and `hi1`/`lo1`/`hi2`/`lo2`. A level is absent when
        its anchor close has no reading.

        **Per horizon** (`horizons[]`): `name`, `minutes` to the settle,
        `em1_pct` (1-sigma, % of spot), `em1` / `em2` (1- and 2-sigma in price),
        `realized_em_pct` (20-day realized vol over the same span). Optional,
        null when not available, and absent on older readings:
        - `up1_pct`, `dn1_pct`, `up2_pct`, `dn2_pct`: the move to each side in %
          of spot as the options' skew prices it (put skew makes the downside
          wider). Null: read `em1_pct` both ways.
        - `tail_src`: how the 2-sigma sides were read: `quantile` (from the
          fitted smile, within the quoted strikes) or `wing` (twice the 1-sigma
          side, which understates a steep tail).
        - `skew_expiry`: the expiration whose smile set that shape.
        - `events[]`: scheduled events inside the horizon (after `asOf`, at or
          before the settle), each `{kind, label, at, timing, jump_pct,
          var_share}`: `kind` is `earnings`, `fomc`, `cpi` or `nfp`; `at` is the
          ISO-8601 instant it is modelled at; earnings add `timing` (`bmo` /
          `amc`), `jump_pct` (the report's own implied move, %) and `var_share`
          (the share of the horizon's priced variance that is the report, 0-1).
        - `event_adjusted`: true when this horizon's move includes an earnings
          report.
        Response: `data.symbols[]` has `symbol`, `asOf`, `sessionDate`, `stale` and `cones`.
        Symbols Tempest does not cover are listed in `data.missing`. **Cost:** 1 credit per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/sigma:
    get:
      operationId: getVolSigma
      x-credits: 1
      summary: Move in units of the implied move (Sigma) per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Tempest Sigma: today's move in units of the one-day move priced at the prior
        close (`running_sigma`), the move budget remaining, theoretical vs
        historical odds of 1- and 2-sigma days, and the last 60 sessions' sigma
        readings (`days`).
        Response: `data.symbols[]` has `symbol`, `asOf`, `sessionDate`, `stale` and `sigma`.
        Symbols Tempest does not cover are listed in `data.missing`. **Cost:** 1 credit per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/surface:
    get:
      operationId: getVolSurface
      x-credits: 3
      summary: Volatility surface and skew per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Tempest Surface: 30-day 25-delta risk reversal (`rr25_30`) and butterfly
        (`bf25_30`), ATM vol, skew percentile over the year and a per-symbol SKEW
        index, plus a smile per expiry (`expiries[]`: strikes/deltas and implied vols).
        Heavier than the headline readings, so priced as analytics.
        Response: `data.symbols[]` has `symbol`, `asOf`, `sessionDate`, `stale` and `surface`.
        Symbols Tempest does not cover are listed in `data.missing`. **Cost:** 3 credits per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/tilt:
    get:
      operationId: getVolTilt
      x-credits: 1
      summary: Call-vs-put premium imbalance (Tilt) per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Tempest Tilt: the one-strike-OTM call vs put premium imbalance at the
        headline expiry as raw and forward-adjusted ratios, which side is cheap,
        its z-score and percentile over the year, each contract's strike, spread
        and distance from its running premium low (percent), and a row per nearby
        expiry. Contract prices (mids, the premium low itself), open interest and
        volume are not served. `liquid` is false on chains too thin to read.
        Response: `data.symbols[]` has `symbol`, `asOf`, `sessionDate`, `stale` and `tilt`.
        Symbols Tempest does not cover are listed in `data.missing`. **Cost:** 1 credit per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/events:
    get:
      operationId: getVolEvents
      x-credits: 1
      summary: Event (earnings) implied move and VRP per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Optional `events.earnings_context` carries the same scheduled-exposure metadata
        documented on `/v1/vol/term`; it is not an earnings-premium estimate.
        Tempest Catalyst: the next earnings date and timing, the move priced into it
        (`implied_move_pct`, from the implied-variance term structure across the event;
        null when only a straddle estimate exists, `estimate: true`), the median and mean past earnings moves and how the
        implied move compares, the report-by-report record, and the volatility risk
        premium (`vrp`: expected VRP and its percentile, 20-day realized vol,
        trailing overpaid share). `events` is null for symbols without a scheduled event.
        Response: `data.symbols[]` has `symbol`, `asOf`, `sessionDate`, `stale` and `events`.
        Symbols Tempest does not cover are listed in `data.missing`. **Cost:** 1 credit per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/snapshot:
    get:
      operationId: getVolSnapshot
      x-credits: 5
      summary: Every Tempest module per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Every per-symbol module in one call: `iv`, `term`, `cones`, `sigma`,
        `surface`, `tilt` and `events` (see each endpoint for the fields).
        **Cost:** 5 credits per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbolsResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/market:
    get:
      operationId: getVolMarket
      x-credits: 1
      summary: The S&P volatility complex
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        The market-wide volatility read: VIX1D, VIX9D, VIX, VIX3M, VIX6M, VVIX
        and SKEW (computed by Tempest from SPX and VIX option chains), their
        ratios and one-year percentiles, the VIX-forward curve state and roll
        (`vx_curve_state`, `vx_roll_pct`, `vx_m1_vs_vix_pct`; the curve's price
        points are not served), regime and crowded-calm flags,
        Mag-7 vs QQQ dispersion, a Fear & Greed score with its components, and
        120 sessions of history for the main series. **Cost:** 1 credit.
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolObjectResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/screener:
    get:
      operationId: getVolScreener
      x-credits: 5
      summary: Screen the whole Tempest universe (Radar)
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Rows can include `earnings_overlap_9d` and `earnings_overlap_30d`, with
        `none`, `partial`, `full`, or null as documented on `/v1/vol/term`.
        These are optional calendar-day exposure labels, not forecast signals.
        Tempest Radar: one row per covered symbol with its headline readings
        (SVX term and percentiles, IV rank, ratio to VIX, term slope, skew,
        tilt, expected move, running sigma and odds, next event and VRP,
        options volume, sector, `quality`). Thin chains are not ranked.
        Filter with `min_<field>` / `max_<field>` on any sortable field, and
        `curve`, `sector`, `quality` (exact match). Unknown parameters are a
        `400`. Rows missing the sort field sort last. **Cost:** 5 credits per
        call (up to 500 rows).
      parameters:
        - name: sort
          in: query
          description: |
            Field to sort by (default `svx30`): svx30, svx1d, svx30_pct_1y,
            svx1d_pct_1y, svx9_pct_1y, svx3m_pct_1y, iv_rank, iv_pct, ratio_vix,
            term_slope, rr25_30, skew_pct_1y, tilt_21, tilt_z, tilt_pct_1y,
            em_1d_pct, running_sigma, sigma_odds_pct, expected_vrp,
            event_move_pct, days_to_event, opt_vol, spot, spot_vol_corr,
            cheap_from_low_pct, day_pace, day_reprice.
            `day_pace` is today's move against the priced one-day move for the
            time elapsed, in sigma; `day_reprice` is the one-day range options
            price now over what they priced at the prior close for the rest of
            the day (above 1: implied vol bid). Both are null outside regular
            hours.
          schema: { type: string, default: svx30 }
        - name: order
          in: query
          schema: { type: string, enum: [asc, desc], default: desc }
        - name: limit
          in: query
          schema: { type: integer, minimum: 1, maximum: 500, default: 50 }
        - name: offset
          in: query
          schema: { type: integer, minimum: 0, default: 0 }
        - name: min_iv_rank
          in: query
          description: Example bound; every sortable field accepts `min_` and `max_`.
          schema: { type: number }
        - name: curve
          in: query
          description: Curve state, e.g. `contango` or `backwardation`.
          schema: { type: string }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolScreenerResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/history:
    get:
      operationId: getVolHistory
      x-credits: 3
      x-credits-per-symbol-day: 0.1
      summary: Daily Tempest history per symbol
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        One row per stored session, at that session's close (15:59 ET): OHLC,
        SVX per tenor and weekend-adjusted, ATM vol, term slope,
        30-day risk reversal / butterfly / ATM vol / skew slope, tilt, chain
        depth (`n_used`), `calc_v`. Columnar: `dates[]` plus one array per
        field in `columns`. Every value was knowable at that session's close;
        features from session D predict D+1 onward. History starts where
        Tempest's backfill does (up to about two years); `/v1/vol/symbols`
        shows each symbol's last stored session.

        **Expected move at each close.** Every row also carries the
        one-standard-deviation (1-sigma) move options priced at that session's
        close for the span to the next session's close, so each past day's
        priced range can be replayed:

        | Column | Meaning |
        |---|---|
        | `em_1d_pct` | The 1-sigma move, in % of that session's close |
        | `em_1d` | The same move in $ (`close * em_1d_pct / 100`) |
        | `range_1d_low` | `close - em_1d` |
        | `range_1d_high` | `close + em_1d` |
        | `em_1d_event` | `1` when an earnings report falls inside the span and its priced move is counted in full, else `0` |

        It is the same next-day move as the Tempest cone at that close: the
        nearest expiry's priced variance, split by trading time, so a Friday
        close prices the weekend. The band is symmetric (no skew). The values
        are `null` where a session has no reading, and for `VIX`.

        **Cost:** per symbol-day: 1 credit per 10 symbol-weekdays in the
        requested window, rounded up, minimum 1 (1 symbol x the default month
        is 3; 10 symbols x one year is 261). Computed from the request, so
        known before the call; holidays are not discounted.
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
        - name: from
          in: query
          description: First session (`YYYY-MM-DD`, ET). Default one month before `to`.
          schema: { type: string, format: date }
        - name: to
          in: query
          description: Last session, inclusive. Default today (ET). At most 800 calendar days after `from`.
          schema: { type: string, format: date }
        - name: fields
          in: query
          description: Comma-separated columns to return (default all).
          schema: { type: string, example: "svx30,svx30_adj,close" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolHistoryResponse" }
              examples:
                expectedMove:
                  summary: SPY, two sessions, fields=close,svx1d,em_1d_pct,em_1d,range_1d_low,range_1d_high,em_1d_event
                  value:
                    data:
                      from: "2026-09-30"
                      to: "2026-10-01"
                      symbols:
                        - symbol: SPY
                          dates: ["2026-09-30", "2026-10-01"]
                          columns:
                            close: [762.34, 764.1]
                            svx1d: [15.2843, 16.5274]
                            em_1d_pct: [0.8003, 0.8654]
                            em_1d: [6.101, 6.6124]
                            range_1d_low: [756.239, 757.4876]
                            range_1d_high: [768.441, 770.7124]
                            em_1d_event: [0, 0]
                      missing: []
                    meta: { module: history, sessionDate: "2026-10-01", marketState: closed, frozen: true, cached: false }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/derived:
    get:
      operationId: getVolDerived
      x-credits: 3
      summary: Realized vs implied and the usual range (one year)
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        The one-year derived series behind the app's charts, per symbol:
        daily SVX30/SVX1D (plain and adjusted), close and risk reversal, the
        point-in-time usual-range band (`p20`/`p50`/`p80`, each day's band
        from the 252 sessions before it), earnings-eve sessions, realized vs
        implied (`ivrv`: 20-day realized vol, VRP series, current VRP and
        percentile), spot-vol correlation and beta, and setups. Updated once
        per session. **Cost:** 3 credits per call (up to 10 symbols).
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolDerivedResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/status:
    get:
      operationId: getVolStatus
      x-credits: 0
      summary: Tempest freshness, coverage and market state (free)
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        When Tempest last computed (`asOf`), the session it belongs to
        (`sessionDate`), whether it is serving the frozen close state
        (`frozen`: outside regular hours nothing is recomputed, because
        after-hours option quotes are too wide to read), the market state now,
        how many symbols are published and coverage counts. Free.
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolObjectResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/symbols:
    get:
      operationId: listVolSymbols
      x-credits: 0
      summary: Symbols covered by Tempest (free)
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Every symbol Tempest publishes, with its latest `asOf` and the last
        stored daily session (`historyThrough`). Free.
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OK.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolObjectResponse" }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
        "504": { $ref: "#/components/responses/GatewayTimeout" }
  /v1/vol/stream:
    get:
      operationId: streamVol
      x-credits: 1
      x-credits-per-minute: 1
      summary: Live Tempest updates (Server-Sent Events)
      tags: [Tempest]
      description: |
        Pushes a symbol's full module state each time Tempest recomputes it:
        about every minute for the most active names and every ~10 minutes for
        the rest during regular hours. Quote readings stay frozen after close;
        calendar or availability updates can still push a full state with the
        same quote timestamp and event ID. Events: `connected`, `vol` (id = asOf in epoch ms; data
        is a `data.symbols[]` element of `/v1/vol/snapshot`), `market` (with
        `market=true`), `credits`, `closed`, `reconnect` (after an hour).
        Resume with `Last-Event-ID` (or `lastEventId`): the initial burst skips
        symbols whose asOf is older than it; a frame at exactly that id may
        repeat. Up to 10 symbols per stream and 5 streams per account. Each
        server also holds a bounded number of open streams across all
        customers; at capacity → `503` `stream_capacity` with `Retry-After: 5`
        (retry; you may land on another server). Access is re-checked every
        minute: a stream closes with `closed` `{"reason":"access_withdrawn"}`
        once the account is no longer enabled.
        **Cost:** 1 credit to connect and 1 per minute open.
      parameters:
        - name: symbols
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Comma-separated Tempest symbols (up to 10). Tempest keys the S&P complex on the option root `SPXW` and Nasdaq-100 on `NDXP`; see `/v1/vol/symbols`.
          schema: { type: string, example: "NVDA,SPY" }
        - name: modules
          in: query
          description: Comma-separated subset of iv, term, cones, sigma, surface, tilt, events (default all).
          schema: { type: string }
        - name: market
          in: query
          description: Also push the market volatility complex.
          schema: { type: boolean, default: false }
        - name: lastEventId
          in: query
          description: Resume point when the client cannot send `Last-Event-ID`.
          schema: { type: integer }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: An SSE stream (`text/event-stream`).
          content:
            text/event-stream:
              schema: { type: string }
        "400": { $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        "401": { $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" }
        "402": { $ref: "#/components/responses/PaymentRequired" }
        "403": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolForbidden" }
        "404": { $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        "429": { $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited" }
        "503": { $ref: "#/components/responses/VolUnavailable" }
  /v1/openapi.json:
    get:
      summary: This OpenAPI specification, as JSON.
      operationId: getOpenAPI
      x-credits: 0
      tags: [Meta]
      description: No key required. Free.
      security: []
      responses:
        "200":
          description: OpenAPI 3.1 document for the Skylit Public API.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { type: object }

components:
  securitySchemes:
    bearerApiKey:
      type: http
      scheme: bearer
      description: |
        Skylit API key in the `Authorization` header
        (`Authorization: Bearer <key>`). The bare key without `Bearer ` is
        also accepted; `X-API-Key` is not.

  parameters:
    Symbols:
      name: symbols
      in: query
      required: true
      description: |
        One ticker, or a comma-separated list for a single cross-asset call
        (e.g. `SPY` or `SPXW,SPY,QQQ`). Each is returned as an element of
        `data.symbols`. At most 10 distinct symbols (more → `400`
        `invalid_parameter`). Unknown symbols in a list are omitted; if none
        is available → `404` `symbol_not_found`.

        Index options are served per option root, and the roots hold
        different contracts. `SPXW` is the PM-settled S&P 500 options (every
        daily and weekly expiration, 0DTE included), the board the Skylit
        app's Trinity view uses. `SPX` is only the AM-settled monthlies, so
        it has no 0DTE or weekly gamma and reads very differently from
        `SPXW`. The same split applies to `NDXP` / `NDX` and `RUTW` / `RUT`.
        To match the app's Trinity or read 0DTE, request `SPXW,SPY,QQQ`.
      schema:
        type: string
        example: SPXW,SPY,QQQ
    Metric:
      name: metric
      in: query
      required: false
      description: Which Greek exposure to return per strike.
      schema:
        type: string
        enum: [gamma, vanna]
        default: gamma
    MaxStrikes:
      name: maxStrikes
      in: query
      required: false
      description: |
        Maximum number of strikes around spot to return: an integer from 1 to
        1000, or `all` for every strike the snapshot lists (SPXW lists about
        730). Values above 1000 return `400 invalid_parameter`; they are never
        silently reduced. Values below 1 are treated as 1. The single-symbol
        stream (`/v1/stream?symbol=`) accepts at most 400 and no `all`.
      schema:
        oneOf:
          - { type: integer, minimum: 1, maximum: 1000 }
          - { type: string, enum: [all] }
        default: 92
    IncludeEmpty:
      name: includeEmpty
      in: query
      required: false
      description: |
        By default, an interior strike whose every returned cell is below 50 in
        absolute value (listed but effectively untraded) is left out, judged on
        the selected metric alone. So gamma and vanna for the same instant can
        return different strike lists. The outermost strikes are never
        removed. `true` keeps every strike in the window, so the list is the
        snapshot's own contiguous ladder and is identical for gamma and vanna.
        Not supported on the single-symbol stream (`symbol=`).
      schema: { type: boolean, default: false }
    Expirations:
      name: expirations
      in: query
      required: false
      description: |
        Net each strike over exactly these expirations (`YYYY-MM-DD`,
        comma-separated) — one for a single-expiration heatmap (`2026-05-22`)
        or several for a custom set (`2026-05-22,2026-06-19`). Supersedes
        `maxExpirations`, and reaches any expiration the snapshot has, not just
        the nearest ones. Requested dates the symbol does not have are ignored;
        the `expirations` array in the response lists what was actually used.
        If none of them match, the response is `404` with
        `code: expiration_not_found` and the available dates in the message.
        On `/v1/heatmap`, expirations that have already expired are not
        available (they are trimmed from the live snapshot) — replay them with
        `/v1/historical` instead.
      schema:
        type: string
        example: "2026-05-22"
    MaxExpirations:
      name: maxExpirations
      in: query
      required: false
      description: |
        How many of the nearest expirations to net into each strike's `value`:
        an integer from 1 to 60, or `all`. Values above 60 return
        `400 invalid_parameter`. Ignored when `expirations` is set.
      schema:
        oneOf:
          - { type: integer, minimum: 1, maximum: 60 }
          - { type: string, enum: [all] }
        default: 5
    Layout:
      name: layout
      in: query
      required: false
      description: |
        `net` (default) returns one net value per strike. `matrix` also returns
        `matrix`, the per-expiration grid those values are summed from.
      schema: { type: string, enum: [net, matrix], default: net }

  schemas:
    LevelsSummary:
      type: object
      description: |
        Digest of the returned strikes for the selected `metric`. Covers only
        the strikes between `lowStrike` and `highStrike` (set by `maxStrikes`,
        `maxExpirations` and `expirations`), never the whole chain.
      required: [netExposure, positiveWall, negativeWall, flip, lowStrike, highStrike]
      properties:
        netExposure:
          type: number
          description: Sum of `value` over the returned strikes.
        positiveWall:
          description: The strike with the largest positive value, or null when none is positive.
          nullable: true
          anyOf:
            - $ref: "#/components/schemas/Level"
            - enum: [null]
        negativeWall:
          description: The strike with the most negative value, or null when none is negative.
          nullable: true
          anyOf:
            - $ref: "#/components/schemas/Level"
            - enum: [null]
        flip:
          description: |
            Where the running sum of `value`, from the lowest returned strike
            upward, changes sign (linear interpolation between the bracketing
            strikes; the crossing nearest spot when there are several). Null
            when the running sum never changes sign within the window.
          nullable: true
          anyOf:
            - type: object
              required: [level, distancePct]
              properties:
                level: { type: number }
                distancePct:
                  type: number
                  description: Percent distance from spot (negative = below).
            - enum: [null]
        lowStrike: { type: number, description: Lowest returned strike. }
        highStrike: { type: number, description: Highest returned strike. }
    Level:
      type: object
      required: [strike, value, nodeType, distancePct]
      properties:
        strike: { type: number }
        value: { type: number, description: Net exposure at this strike for the selected metric. }
        nodeType: { type: string, enum: [king, gatekeeper, pika, barney, significant] }
        distancePct: { type: number, description: Percent distance from spot (negative = below). }
    SymbolHeatmap:
      type: object
      required: [symbol, asOf, spot, previousClose, priceChange, priceChangePercent, expirations, strikes]
      properties:
        symbol: { type: string, description: Canonical ticker for the returned data. }
        asOf:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          description: RFC3339 timestamp of the snapshot actually returned (nearest to the requested instant).
        spot:
          type: number
          description: |
            On `/v1/heatmap`, the latest underlying price at the time of the
            request, which can be newer than the board. On `/v1/historical`
            and in stream frames, the spot the board was computed at. The
            board's own spot is `previousClose + priceChange`.
        previousClose: { type: number }
        priceChange: { type: number, description: "The board's spot minus previous close (the board's spot, not `spot`, on `/v1/heatmap`)." }
        priceChangePercent: { type: number }
        expirations:
          type: array
          description: Expiration dates (YYYY-MM-DD) contributing to each strike's net value.
          items: { type: string, format: date }
        strikes:
          type: array
          description: Per-strike nodes, ordered by strike ascending.
          items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/StrikeNode" }
        matrix:
          type: array
          description: |
            Present only with `layout=matrix`. One row per entry in `strikes`,
            one column per entry in `expirations`: `matrix[i][j]` is the
            exposure at strike i for expiration j.
          items: { type: array, items: { type: number } }

    StrikeNode:
      type: object
      required: [strike, value, nodeType]
      properties:
        strike: { type: number, description: Strike price. }
        value:
          type: number
          description: Net exposure for the selected `metric` at this strike (summed across the returned expirations).
        nodeType:
          type: string
          description: Skylit's node classification for this strike.
          enum: [king, gatekeeper, pika, barney, significant, normal]
        velocityPct:
          type: number
          description: |
            Live percent change of this strike's value over the velocity window.
            Present on `/v1/heatmap` only; omitted on `/v1/historical`.

    Meta:
      type: object
      required: [metric, resolution, mode, cached]
      properties:
        metric: { type: string, enum: [gamma, vanna] }
        resolution:
          type: string
          enum: ["1s", "1m"]
          description: |
            Time resolution of the data served: "1s" when every symbol came
            from 1-second data, "1m" when any came from minute-resolution
            history.
          example: "1s"
        mode: { type: string, enum: [live, historical] }
        cached: { type: boolean, description: True if served from the in-process cache. }
        delayed:
          type: boolean
          description: |
            True when your plan's data is delayed and this latest-data request
            was served as of `delayMinutes` ago (mode is then `historical`).
            Absent on real-time plans.
        delayMinutes: { type: integer, description: The delay applied when `delayed` is true. }
        attribution:
          allOf: [{ $ref: "#/components/schemas/Attribution" }]
          description: |
            How to credit this data. Most routes send the short form
            `{text, url, terms}` ("Data: Skylit"). Routes whose data class the
            licensing design (TERMS.md §5) tags explicitly — today,
            `/v1/options/*` — send the full licensing shape instead. Can be
            absent; do not infer sharing rules from the short form or from
            its absence.

    Attribution:
      type: object
      required: [text, url]
      description: |
        Whether and how this response's data may be published. See
        `/legal/api#sharing`. An Agent or MCP client should never publish
        data where `shareable` is false, regardless of `shareClass`.
        `required`, `license`, `shareable` and `shareClass` are always sent
        on `/v1/options/*` and absent from the short form.
      properties:
        text: { type: string, example: "Powered by Skylit" }
        url: { type: string, format: uri }
        required: { type: boolean }
        license: { type: string, enum: [personal, commercial, connected_app] }
        shareable: { type: boolean }
        shareClass:
          type: string
          enum: [derived, derived_levels_only, raw]
          description: "\"raw\" (e.g. option quotes, greeks) must never be auto-published."
        terms: { type: string, format: uri }

    SymbolRange:
      type: object
      required: [symbol, axes, frames]
      properties:
        symbol: { type: string, description: Canonical ticker for the returned data. }
        axes:
          type: array
          description: Strike/expiration axes referenced by `frames[].axis`.
          items:
            type: object
            required: [id, strikes, expirations]
            properties:
              id: { type: integer }
              strikes:
                type: array
                description: Visible strikes, ascending.
                items: { type: number }
              expirations:
                type: array
                description: Expirations (YYYY-MM-DD) netted into each value.
                items: { type: string, format: date }
        frames:
          type: array
          description: Snapshots in the window, oldest first.
          items:
            type: object
            required: [asOf, axis, spot, previousClose, values]
            properties:
              asOf: { type: string, format: date-time, description: Snapshot instant (millisecond precision). }
              axis: { type: integer, description: Id of the axis in `axes` these values are aligned to. }
              spot: { type: number }
              previousClose: { type: number }
              values:
                type: array
                description: Net exposure per strike, aligned with the axis's `strikes`.
                items: { type: number }
    DailyStat:
      type: object
      required: [date, frames, complete, firstAt, lastAt, spotOpen, spotHigh, spotLow, spotClose, minValue, maxValue, peakAbsMean, peakAbsMax]
      properties:
        date: { type: string, format: date, description: "The trading session's date (ET)." }
        frames: { type: integer, description: 1-minute frames inside the session the values are computed from. }
        complete: { type: boolean, description: False for a session still in progress (today) or ended less than 30 minutes ago. }
        firstAt: { type: string, format: date-time }
        lastAt: { type: string, format: date-time }
        spotOpen: { type: number }
        spotHigh: { type: number }
        spotLow: { type: number }
        spotClose: { type: number }
        minValue: { type: number, description: Smallest single cell (strike x expiration) in any frame. }
        maxValue: { type: number, description: Largest single cell in any frame. }
        peakAbsMean: { type: number, description: "Mean over frames of max(|smallest cell|, |largest cell|)." }
        peakAbsMax: { type: number, description: "Maximum over frames of max(|smallest cell|, |largest cell|)." }

    VolMeta:
      type: object
      required: [module, marketState, frozen, cached]
      properties:
        module: { type: string, description: "Which endpoint answered (iv, cones, screener, ...)." }
        asOf: { type: string, format: date-time, description: "When Tempest computed the newest value in this response." }
        sessionDate: { type: string, format: date, description: "The trading session (ET) that asOf belongs to. The close state is stamped 15:59 ET and always belongs to its own session." }
        marketState: { type: string, enum: [pre_open, open, post_close, closed], description: "US equity session at request time." }
        frozen: { type: boolean, description: "True while Tempest serves the previous close (outside regular hours)." }
        publishedAt: { type: string, format: date-time, description: "When Tempest last published to the API." }
        cached: { type: boolean }
        attribution: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Attribution" }
    VolMissing:
      type: object
      required: [symbol, reason]
      properties:
        symbol: { type: string }
        reason: { type: string, enum: [not_covered, no_history] }
    VolSymbol:
      type: object
      required: [symbol, asOf, sessionDate, stale]
      description: |
        One symbol. Besides these fields it carries the requested module(s)
        as objects keyed `iv`, `term`, `cones`, `sigma`, `surface`, `tilt`,
        `events` (null when Tempest has none for the symbol). Module field
        names follow Tempest's own (snake_case). Quote-derived prices (fields
        named `mid`, `*_mid`, `straddle*`, `forward`, `price`, and a contract's
        `low`, `oi`, `vol`) are never present.
      properties:
        symbol: { type: string }
        asOf: { type: string, format: date-time }
        sessionDate: { type: string, format: date }
        stale: { type: boolean, description: "In session, true when the reading is more than 20 minutes old." }
      additionalProperties: true
    VolSymbolsResponse:
      type: object
      required: [data, meta]
      properties:
        data:
          type: object
          required: [symbols, missing]
          properties:
            symbols: { type: array, items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolSymbol" } }
            missing: { type: array, items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMissing" } }
        meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMeta" }
    VolObjectResponse:
      type: object
      required: [data, meta]
      properties:
        data: { type: object, additionalProperties: true }
        meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMeta" }
    VolScreenerResponse:
      type: object
      required: [data, meta]
      properties:
        data:
          type: object
          required: [rows, total, offset, limit, sort]
          properties:
            rows: { type: array, items: { type: object, additionalProperties: true } }
            total: { type: integer, description: "Rows matching the filters, before offset/limit." }
            offset: { type: integer }
            limit: { type: integer }
            sort: { type: string }
        meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMeta" }
    VolHistoryResponse:
      type: object
      required: [data, meta]
      properties:
        data:
          type: object
          required: [symbols, missing, from, to]
          properties:
            from: { type: string, format: date }
            to: { type: string, format: date }
            symbols:
              type: array
              items:
                type: object
                required: [symbol, dates, columns]
                properties:
                  symbol: { type: string }
                  dates: { type: array, items: { type: string, format: date } }
                  columns:
                    type: object
                    additionalProperties: { type: array, items: { type: number, nullable: true } }
            missing: { type: array, items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMissing" } }
        meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMeta" }
    VolDerivedResponse:
      type: object
      required: [data, meta]
      properties:
        data:
          type: object
          required: [symbols, missing]
          properties:
            symbols:
              type: array
              items:
                type: object
                required: [symbol, derived]
                properties:
                  symbol: { type: string }
                  derived: { type: object, additionalProperties: true }
            missing: { type: array, items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMissing" } }
        meta: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/VolMeta" }
    Error:
      type: object
      required: [error]
      properties:
        error:
          type: object
          required: [code, message]
          properties:
            code:
              type: string
              description: Stable, machine-readable error code.
              example: no_data
            message:
              type: string
              description: Human-readable explanation.

    StreamSnapshot:
      description: /v1/stream v2 `snapshot` event payload — a SymbolHeatmap (without per-strike velocityPct) plus `lagged`.
      allOf:
        - $ref: "#/components/schemas/SymbolHeatmap"
        - type: object
          required: [lagged]
          properties:
            lagged:
              type: boolean
              description: True when newer boards replaced ones this client had not yet received (slow reader); this is the newest.
    StreamVelocity:
      description: /v1/stream v2 `velocity` event payload.
      type: object
      properties:
        symbol: { type: string }
        metric: { type: string, enum: [gamma, vanna] }
        asOf: { type: string, format: date-time }
        nodes:
          type: array
          items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/NodeVelocity" }
        topRisers:
          type: array
          items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/NodeVelocity" }
        topFallers:
          type: array
          items: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/NodeVelocity" }
    NodeVelocity:
      type: object
      properties:
        strike: { type: number }
        expiration: { type: string }
        currentValue: { type: number }
        delta1Min: { type: number }
        delta5Min: { type: number }
        delta10Min: { type: number }
        delta15Min: { type: number }
        delta1Hour: { type: number }
        delta4Hour: { type: number }
        delta1Day: { type: number }
        percent1Min: { type: number }
        percent5Min: { type: number }
        percent10Min: { type: number }
        percent15Min: { type: number }
        percent1Hour: { type: number }
        percent4Hour: { type: number }
        percent1Day: { type: number }
        velocity: { type: number, description: Average change per minute over 5 minutes. }
        trend: { type: string, enum: [increasing, decreasing, stable] }
        history: { type: array, items: { type: number } }
    StreamResumed:
      description: /v1/stream v2 `resumed` event payload.
      type: object
      properties:
        lastEventId: { type: string }
        gapCovered: { type: boolean, description: True only if no symbol had a board published during the gap. }
        stateRestored: { type: boolean, description: True when every symbol received a current snapshot. }
        symbols:
          type: array
          items:
            type: object
            properties:
              symbol: { type: string }
              status: { type: string, enum: [unchanged, advanced, unknown, unavailable] }
              lastAsOf: { type: string, format: date-time }
              currentAsOf: { type: string, format: date-time }
  responses:
    PaymentRequired:
      description: Out of credits (`insufficient_credits`).
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    BadRequest:
      description: Request validation failed.
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    Unauthorized:
      description: Missing API key (`unauthorized`), sent by the gateway.
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    Forbidden:
      description: |
        Unknown, revoked or expired key (`forbidden`, from the gateway), or an
        admin-suspended account (`account_suspended`).
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    NotFound:
      description: |
        Unknown symbol, no data available, or none of the requested
        `expirations` exist for the symbol (`code: expiration_not_found`).
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    RateLimited:
      description: Per-minute rate limit exceeded.
      headers: { Retry-After: { schema: { type: integer } } }
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    Unavailable:
      description: Heatmap data is temporarily unavailable.
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    VolForbidden:
      description: |
        As `Forbidden`, or `not_entitled`: Tempest data is not enabled for this
        account (it is in preview). Refunded.
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    VolUnavailable:
      description: Tempest data is loading (`warming_up`, with `Retry-After`) or not configured (`unavailable`). Refunded.
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
    GatewayTimeout:
      description: |
        The request did not finish in time (`gateway_timeout`). Refunded;
        retry, or narrow the request.
      content: { application/json: { schema: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error" } } }
